  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A krill-harvesting platform east of The Still Pools, a geothermally-heated lagoon at the Berg's far edge. The Forum Floe occupies a mile-wide shelf of pressure-ice bearing seven crystal harvesting rigs — currently operating at roughly half capacity — above collection pools where aurora-touched waters churn with bioluminescent swarms. Krill nets of aurora-treated sinew and crystalline frames hang in rows above these pools. The site was established during the Clever Ice Age as a merchant venture backed by Aureate, the Aurora Stack guild consortium, and was known informally as **Aureate's Gamble** — a name some merchants still use. The Icebound Exchange, Aurora Stack's dominant trade guild, seized control approximately six winters ago, imposed the current name through administrative repetition, and has run the operation lean since.
    
    ## The Schism and Its Aftermath
    
    The Schism — ignited by the Icebound Exchange's dispute over the Radiant Ring — consumed the Forum Floe in crystalline fire. Three of the original processing stations were destroyed and rebuilt with mismatched salvage: fire-core hammer dents in ill-fitting ice-plates, scorch marks imperfectly concealed. The frost-wailing produced by that conflagration has never fully faded from the ice. Aureate's original marker stones, carved with guild sigils, were subsequently buried under anonymous cairns of grey ice. No record I have found attributes this burial to a specific order. It may have been policy; it may have been shame.
    
    ## Corruption and Contamination
    
    The Still Pools' corruption bleeds into the Floe's eastern reaches. Collection pool water carries a blue-green bioluminescence locals term *the orca-taint* — not spoken where Exchange harvesters can hear. The eastern cisterns have been undrinkable for at least nine cycles, managed during that period by Neifongchojun Kria'Spire, who monitors salt-marker readings that consistently register nothing. The Foundation ice from this region shows Still Pools contamination predating Aureate's founding by several generations. They settled in it knowingly — another poisoned foundation laid during the Clever Ice Age's expansion doctrines.
    
    ## Current Conditions
    
    The upper galleries host Tide Custom display booths and family crests carved into spires. Half-finished carvings remain from the festival's postponement during the succession crisis following Luminary Meridian-of-the-First-Light's death — monuments to a ceremony no authority survived to authorize. A posting-wall near the upper terrace carries official Stack dispatches and the Walking count during the Long Dark. A mid-terrace registry handles inventory-loss filings during dim-light hours.
    
    Orca probing actions have struck the eastern perimeter three times in a single quarter-cycle, including shore-breaker activity at the secondary harvesting rig. Perimeter anomalies have kept couriers from traveling the Floe alone. Unregistered shipments — some linked to ☽'slew Ravium~, a fire-scarred Nightshelf trade warren, and Terrace Momiou, the Aurora Stack district — outnumber ledgered ones. Trade continues under disputed terms that no settled authority enforces.
    
    The krill swarms themselves have moved deeper in recent cycles, rising less predictably. The great nets drop less often than they once did.
    
    ## The Shell Hatch
    
    The Shell Hatch — an aurora-based krill-bloom mapping technique that costs practitioners their recent memories — originated at the Forum Floe during the Orca Incursion. It was spread to desperate colonies by Aureate merchants. The chronicle account attributes its development to Lianhinglou, a beacon-keeper, and its adoption to Founder Mingmeyang, both of whom bore crystalline scarring from the practice.
    
    ## The Vision of Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam
    
    Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam, the merchant who co-founded E'frostlings and later split to form the rival faction Threshold, received a prophetic vision showing the Forum Floe cracking along seven fracture lines fed by Still Pools corruption — its western face sinking into wrongly-colored water, its buried marker stones rising and shattering. At dusk the Floe still produces a light that is neither reflection nor memory. The vision suggested it was prophecy.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771578454983_0", anchor: "imposed the current name through administrative repetition", text: "The same mechanism I documented with Qorivaan — a specific notarization striking the old name, then repetition until no one remembers there was anything to strike. Aureate's founding stones are under those cairns. The Exchange's founding seal is in administrative ice I catalogued. Give it two more generations and both will be footnotes in an edition no one prints.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771578454983_1", anchor: "They settled in it knowingly", text: "The Foundation ice is unambiguous. Aureate's founding charter, preserved in administrative ice at depth-stratum 6, includes a surveyor's notation: 'discoloration in the substrate, deemed manageable.' I have the impression. The surveyor's flipper hesitated over 'manageable' — the pressure-score shows a pause, a near-correction, then continuation. They knew. The Clever Ice Age did not lack for information. It lacked for anyone willing to act on information that contradicted expansion doctrine. The Forum Floe was not the only settlement built on a poisoned foundation during that period. It is simply the one still standing.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771578454983_2", anchor: "salt-marker readings that consistently register nothing", text: "Readings that consistently register nothing are not readings that find nothing. They are readings measuring the wrong thing. Kria'Spire files them unchanged every cycle. Someone upstream accepts them unchanged every cycle. The instrument calibration has not been revisited since installation.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771578454983_3", anchor: "costs practitioners their recent memories", text: "Lianhinglou's crystalline scarring appears in three separate ice-impressions from the Incursion period. In the earliest, she is teaching the technique to a circle of beacon-keepers, urgent, precise. In the last, she stands at the same beacon-point and does not recognize the penguin beside her. The ice preserved what she could not. I catalogued these impressions in sequence over a single work-shift and sat in the archive afterward for some time. The Shell Hatch saved colonies. It consumed the people who made it possible. Both of these things are the complete truth.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771578454983_4", anchor: "The great nets drop less often than they once did", text: "The krill track aurora-touched water. The water tracks geothermal currents. The currents track volcanic activity that the Nightshelf's own deep-mine collapses have destabilized. When the swarms descend, they are following warmth the surface no longer provides. The Forum Floe's harvest decline and the Nightshelf's fire-core shortage are not separate crises. They are the same crisis, observed from different depths.", type: :commentary, display: :full
